  "narrative": {
    "text": "Figure 1. A planning chart in seven coloured rows, one per phase of planning and implementing digital health: 01 assessing the current state and enabling environment, 02 establishing a shared understanding and strategic planning, 03 defining the future state, 04 planning the enterprise architecture, 05 determining health content requirements, 06 M&E of digital health implementations and fostering data use, 07 implementing, maintaining and scaling. Each row lists its steps, then the WHO, ITU and partner tools that support it (among them the WHO-ITU National eHealth Strategy Toolkit, the DIIG, OpenHIE, TOGAF, WHO SMART Guidelines' digital adaptation kits, ICD-11 and HL7 FHIR). A dashed box at the right, 'WHO-ITU Reference Architecture for DPI-H', spans the phases. A footnote expands the abbreviations HIS, ICT, ITU, M&E and SDG.",
